===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro}} {{term|trebuchet|lang=fro}}, {{term|trebuket}} et al. (modern {{term|trébuchet}}), from {{term|trabucher||to overthrow}}, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|trabuchare}}.

===Pronunciation===
*{{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈtɹɛbəʃɛt/|/ˈtɹɛbuːʃeɪ/}}
*{{a|US}} {{enPR|trěb’yə-sat}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A medieval [[siege engine]] consisting of a large pivoting arm heavily weighted on one end.  Considered to be the technological successor to the [[catapult]].

